{"abstract":[{"text":"Load centrality (Goh, Kahng and Kim 2001; Brandes 2008): from every source s, each vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"t ≠ s sends one unit to s along shortest paths, a vertex splitting what reaches it equally","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"among its shortest-path predecessors (each parallel copy one); a vertex’s load is what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"passes through it as neither end, summed over ordered pairs (s, t). It differs from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"betweenness, which splits in proportion to the number of shortest paths. ","type":"text"},{"code":"normalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"divides by (n − 1)(n − 2); there is no scaling when n ≤ 2, and an unnormalized sum counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both orders of each pair. Self-loops never matter. O(nm).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Centrality\/documentation\/Centrality","doc:\/\/Centrality\/documentation\/Centrality\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Centrality\/documentation\/Centrality\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Centrality\/documentation\/Centrality\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/loadCentrality(normalized:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/centrality\/graphprotocols\/graph\/loadcentrality(normalized:)"]}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","title":"loadCentrality(normalized:)","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P10CentralityE04loadC010normalizedAD0C6ScoresVyAA12DirectedViewVyxGGSb_tF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"loadCentrality","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier